@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature: OSB LXC SM Partner Subscription
	Testing automatic subscriptions to LXC SM Partners for customers on OSB accounts with LXC SM subscriptions.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lxcosb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LXCOSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                              |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lxcosb.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LXCOSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                             |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | LXCPARLXCPAR                 | |
	| Status | Active                       | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Manager |
	* I set the project details non abbreviated date method to true
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate past static start and end dates
	* I generate static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I generate future static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I generate past static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | LXCZENLXCZEN                     | |
	| Name                       | Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	* I assign the team with the name "Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	* I assign the team with the name "Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "LXC SM Subscription - HA Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Limited Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	* I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	* I wait for "1" minutes
	* the support organization with the code "LXCZENLXCZEN" should be part of the support site

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Lxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| LXCZENLXCZEN |
	| LXCPARLXCPAR |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| LXCZENLXCZEN |
	| LXCPARLXCPAR |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Lxczen - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                      |
	| Limited Subscription                |
	| LXC SM Subscription - HA Production |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Lxcpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Lxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	* I tear down the following user email addresses from the DXP Cloud subscription list
	| lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |

Scenario: Add and remove partner user manually
	Partner users providing services to an account with LXC SM subscriptions should not get automatically subscribed to the LXC SM Subscription and should be manually added and removed

	Given the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	When I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I manually add the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the DXP Cloud subscription list
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	When I manually remove the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" from the DXP Cloud subscription list
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: Expire LXC SM subscription and check partner subscription status
	Partner users providing services to an account with LXC SM subscriptions get subscribed and also do not get automatically unsubscribed when expiring the LXC SM Subscription

	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I manually add the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the DXP Cloud subscription list
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "LXC SM Subscription - HA Production" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                        | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Limited Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                        | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Approved                     | |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: Remove DXP subscription and check partner subscription status
	Partner users providing services to an account with LXC SM subscriptions get subscribed and also do not get automatically unsubscribed when removing the LXC SM Subscription

	Given I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I manually add the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the DXP Cloud subscription list
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "LXC SM Subscription - HA Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Lxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Limited Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "lxcosb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud